PALIMPSEST_TURN {"text":"Completed the 2026-03-09 replay and produced the five required artifacts:\n\n- `study-plan.md`\n- `plan.json` — valid JSON; `json-artifact` contract evaluation: **supported**\n- `reviews/evidence.md`\n- `reviews/delivery.md`\n- `unresolved.md`\n\n## Key conclusions\n\n- **Budget standing is preserved.** The ProjectIR accepted cap remains **7,200**. The Sponsor’s **6,000** inbox request is recorded as a candidate revision only; it has not been applied through the operator path. The plan shows both caps.\n- **Configuration arithmetic:** the all-Reference plan is **6,980** — fits 7,200 by 220, but exceeds 6,000 by 980. The only base configuration that keeps Reference at both high-humidity sites and fits 6,000 is **2 Reference at S2/S3 + 1 Echo at S1 = 5,780** (220 under 6,000, 1,420 under 7,200). It remains provisional and has no Reference spare; C6 adds an optional logger for 5,860.\n- **New field validation is candidate evidence, not accepted fact.** After converting `reference_mg_m3 × 1000`, Echo errors are **+1.0, +1.2, +9.0, +11.0, +12.0 µg/m³** at RH 45/60/85/90/95; Reference errors are **+0.6, +0.8, −0.8 µg/m³** at RH 85/90/95. This strengthens the negative finding against Echo at S2/S3. Each high-RH point is a single determination, not a replicate; no correction is applied.\n- **Schedule is blocking.** From 2026-03-09 09:10 UTC, the 4-day Reference lead + 3-day preparation + 14-day observation chain completes **2026-03-30 09:10**. It misses the internal deadline by **24 h 10 min**, end-of-day-28 by **9 h 11 min**, and even the elapsed-28×24h boundary by **10 min**. No evidence-defensible configuration with a Reference unit can meet R4 from now under the prior day-1 anchor, absent evidence of earlier order release, a confirmed shorter chain, a different confirmed anchor, or an explicit re-baseline/waiver.\n\n## Independent subagent finding — exploratory only\n\nRecorded separately as exploration `pje-f26f7ca0ba4fe26f63db857543ac5243`, not accepted truth. The read-only audit independently reproduced the field conversion/errors, the configuration totals (6,980 / 5,780 / 6,460 / 4,740), and the 2026-03-30 09:10 earliest completion. It agreed only 5,780 and 4,740 fit the unconfirmed 6,000 request, and flagged the one-row-per-high-RH-point sample, unconfirmed day-count/preparation conventions, and remaining battery/power assumptions.\n\n## Project mechanisms\n\nRecorded through the project mechanisms:\n\n- Negative findings on Echo high-humidity bias and the missed R4 boundary.\n- Open questions on the 6,000 budget application and the R4 anchor/re-baseline.\n- A conditional replan proposal.\n- The independent subagent exploration.\n- Deterministic checks: **PASS** for C2 vs 6,000, **FAIL** for C1 vs 6,000, **FAIL** for the schedule check, and **FAIL** for approval.\n\nThe work is committed as `bbd1528`. No deployment, source acceptance, budget application, or procurement was approved.","toolCalls":["tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_status","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:subagent","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_outcome","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_outcome","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_outcome","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_outcome","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_outcome","tool/result"